# Task Routing

The eight specialist `rd-*` research and document skills can be used independently and in any order. They are not a forced pipeline. `/rd-delivery` is an explicit orchestrator for multi-artifact work, not a mandatory first stage.

## Available Skills

| Skill | Deliverable | Daily work |
|---|---|---|
| `/rd-requirement` | Structured requirements / PRD / SRS | Requirements analysis and product/design input |
| `/rd-feasibility` | Feasibility study / feasibility analysis report | Project feasibility and decision support |
| `/rd-research` | Evidence package / research notes / fact-check matrix | Standards, open source, AI tools, configuration behavior, and contested claims |
| `/rd-solution` | Technical proposal / high-level design / construction plan | System architecture and solution documentation |
| `/rd-design` | Detailed design document | Interface, data, flow, error, security, and concurrency design |
| `/rd-specification` | Standards/specification draft or clause revision | Standards formulation, revision, and normative wording work |
| `/rd-writing` | Technical article / evidence report / decision brief | Audience-ready, source-backed professional writing |
| `/rd-review` | Independent review findings | Engineering documents, research reports, standards, and article review |
| `/rd-delivery` | Delivery charter / artifact map / phase gates / handoff | Explicit multi-stage and cross-session orchestration |

## Authoring To Review Mapping

| Authoring skill | Review skill | Review mode |
|---|---|---|
| `/rd-requirement` to PRD / SRS | `/rd-review` | Requirements Review |
| `/rd-feasibility` to feasibility report | `/rd-review` | Feasibility Review |
| `/rd-solution` to proposal / high-level design / construction plan | `/rd-review` | Proposal Review |
| `/rd-design` to detailed design | `/rd-review` | Design Review |
| `/rd-specification` to standard / specification / clause draft | `/rd-review` | Standards Review |
| `/rd-writing` to technical article / evidence report / decision brief | `/rd-review` | Article Review |

`/rd-research` is not part of the authoring-to-review chain. Use it as evidence input for `/rd-feasibility`, `/rd-solution`, `/rd-specification`, `/rd-design`, `/rd-writing`, or fact-dependent `/rd-review`. Research reports and technology evaluations can themselves use Research Review mode. Use `/rd-delivery` only when the user explicitly requests cross-artifact orchestration, phase gates, or a durable handoff.

## Invocation Guidance

- Invoke the relevant skill by name when the task clearly matches it.
- Do not force a full PRD-to-design pipeline for small tasks.
- For reviews, lead with severity-graded findings.
- For standards work, cite exact clauses and mark missing evidence as requiring human verification.
- For feasibility work, separate facts, assumptions, estimates, and unknowns.
- Use `/rd-research` when a material evidence gap needs its specialist workflow; keep routine supporting checks in the primary workflow. Use `/rd-writing` for audience-ready narrative and `/rd-review` for an independent verdict.
- Use `/rd-delivery` only for explicit multi-document or cross-session coordination; route a single deliverable directly.
- For an explicitly requested `/rd-delivery` engagement, read and follow the [rd-delivery Skill](../skills/rd-delivery/SKILL.md) for its artifact-authority and phase-gate contract. General authorization and evidence boundaries remain applicable to all tasks.

## Parallel Work

Use parallel or background work only when subtasks are independent, write scopes do not overlap, and the outputs can be merged without ambiguity.
